{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And Abraham drew near.</b> We find drawing near for battle — ״וַיִּגַּשׁ יוֹאָב״ (II Samuel 10); and drawing near for appeasement — ״וַיִּגַּשׁ אֵלָיו יְהוּדָה״; and drawing near for prayer — ״וַיִּגַּשׁ אֵלִיָּהוּ הַנָּבִיא״ (I Kings 18). And into all of these Abraham entered — to speak harshly, and to appease, and to pray." "<b>Will You even sweep away.</b> הַאַף תִּסְפֶּה. And for the Targum of Onkelos, which translates it as an expression of anger — thus is its meaning: will anger move You to sweep away the righteous with the wicked?"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:59:19.474371971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}